cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this bench, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mdaa_bench: simulation bench for blind identification of latent dynamical structure (MDAA)"
version: v4.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hudsonbonomo/mdaa_bench"
authors:
  - family-names: Bonomo
    given-names: Hudson A. R.
    affiliation: "TMU-LAB — The Machine Unconscious Lab, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0656-7641"
abstract: >-
  Test bench in which trajectories are generated from known lattice nodes, observed
  through a noisy and irregularly sampled observation map, and handed blind to an
  identification pipeline. The output is a recovery map: how often the pipeline
  recovers the planted node, activates a spurious axis, or misses a planted one,
  across measurement noise, series length, sampling density and observation
  nonlinearity. The bench validates the pipeline, never the construct.
keywords:
  - dynamical systems
  - system identification
  - state-space models
  - switching linear systems
  - simulation benchmark
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
  - MDAA
